<title>CHINA: Tobacco, oil, minerals and drugs reap China profit.</title>
<headline>Tobacco, oil, minerals and drugs reap China profit.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's five most profitable industries are tobacco processing, oil and gas refining, oil and gas extraction, exploitation of non-ferrous metals and pharmaceutical production, the Financial News said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>A national survey of 40 major industries had discovered that all of the five top money-making sectors were capital intensive and enjoyed return on capital and net return on assets of more than 10 percent, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The tobacco industry -- China's biggest tax-paying sector -- topped the list of high earning industries with a return on capital rate of 49.32 percent and a net return on assets rate of 27.69 percent, it said.</p>
<p>Aside from being capital-intensive, three of the top industries -- pharmaceuticals, oil and gas extraction and refining -- also required heavy emphasis on technology, it said but gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
